 This guide describes the specific rules for complying with Klarna’s network requirements.
 
-## Prohibited business categories
+## Prohibited business categories 
 
 In addition to the industry and business categories listed in [Prohibited and restricted business](https://stripe.com/restricted-businesses), you can’t use Klarna for the following categories:
 
 - Charities
 - Political organizations, parties, or initiatives
-- B2B
+- Business-to-business (BTB)
+- Money services: Binary options, cash disbursements, foreign currency, currency exchange, money transfer, digital and crypto currencies, crypto exchanges, tokens, and other crypto assets
+- Stored value cards, vouchers and gift cards
+- Bailiffs, bankruptcy and insolvency services, fines, claims management, and debt collection management agencies
+- Court costs, bail and bond payments, and fines
+- Gambling, betting, or lotteries (includes government-owned lotteries)
+- Direct marketing (for example, inbound telemarketing)
+- Fund-raising organizations (includes crowd funding platforms)
 
 For more information about Klarna eligibility for your account, navigate to your [Payment methods settings](https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/payment_methods).
 
